# Export engine parity (PDF + Office)

Canonical lessons: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-05-pdf-office-engine-qol.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-09-05-pdf-office-engine-qol.md).
Roadmap: [`docs/audit/future-pdf-and-docx-engines-2026-08.md`](../../docs/audit/future-pdf-and-docx-engines-2026-08.md).

## Three lanes

| Lane | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `pdf-export.ts` (raster) | Canvas Comms print (Flyer, Board Notice, …) |
| `text-pdf-layout.ts` + `pdf-layout/` | Selectable worksheets, certificates, Hub reports |
| `office-export.ts` + builders + `ooxml-font-embed.ts` | Editable DOCX / XLSX / PPTX |

Do **not** merge raster + text PDF into one writer. Share Brand Kit font resolution, OFL binaries, and `downloadBlob` / export success UX instead.

## Must do on new/changed Office exports

1. Resolve faces via `resolveOfficeBrandFonts` / `canvasFontOfficeName` (`office-brand-styles.ts`).
2. DOCX/PPTX: `embedDocxBrandFonts` / `embedPptxBrandFonts` after build (catalog ids; system faces no-op).
3. XLSX: `withOfficeXlsxFont` on header/title cells.
4. Steward-facing sheet chrome: EN/FR label packs; COUNTIF + data-validation strings use the same tokens.
5. UI downloads: `downloadBlob` — no one-off `createObjectURL` helpers in Hub boards.
6. Tests: blob size; embed → `listEmbeddedOoxmlFonts`; XLSX → `font.name` + localized labels.

## PDF

- Floor handouts → text PDF layout (no private jsPDF letter loops).
- New canvas tools → raster path + capture fidelity.
- Guide PDF chrome: [`.cursor/rules/guide-pdfs.mdc`](guide-pdfs.mdc).

## Verify before editing symbols

Prefer a byte-level listing of `export function` / `export type` in the target file before imports — search paraphrases have drifted identifiers in this repo before.

```bash
npm run test:unit -- src/lib/export/office-brand-styles.test.ts src/lib/export/office-export.test.ts src/lib/minutes/export-docx.test.ts src/lib/elections/export-ballot.test.ts
```
